.TH MOUNTPILOT "8" "May 2026" "MountPilot sumo 2.0.2" "System Administration Utilities"
.SH NAME
MountPilot \- A mount and monitoring tool for heterogeneous data sources
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B sumo
\fI\,OPTIONS <block device path | disk file name| overlay path | ADB URL | NFS URL | FTP URL | SSH URL | SAMBA URL | UNC address | HTTP address> \/\fR[\fI\,<mount folder>\/\fR]
.br
.B sumo
\fI\,OPTIONS -L|--label= <volume label> \/\fR[\fI\,<mount folder>\/\fR]
.br
.B sumo
\fI\,OPTIONS -u <mount point folder>\/\fR
.br
.B sumo
\fI\,OPTIONS -u -L <volume label>\/\fR
.br
.B sumo
\fI\,OPTIONS -u <block device path | disk file name| overlay path | ADB URL | NFS URL | FTP URL | SSH URL | SAMBA URL | UNC address | HTTP address>\/\fR
.br
.B sumo
\fI\,OPTIONS -F|--format-disk -t <filesystem type> <block device path>\/\fR
.br
.B sumo
\fI\,OPTIONS -B|--flash-disk= <disk image> <block device path>\/\fR
.br
.B sumo
\fI\,OPTIONS -P|--part-disk= <partition GUID>\/\fR
.br
.B sumo
\fI\,OPTIONS \/\fR[\fI\,-l\/\fR] [\fI\,coma-separated list of filter names\/\fR]
.br
.B sumo
\fI\,OPTIONS \/\fR[\fI\,-i\/\fR]
.PP
Arguments:
.TP
<block device path>
e.g. \fI\,/dev/sda\/\fP, \fI\,/dev/sdb1\/\fP, \fI\,/dev/loop23\/\fP
.TP
<disk file>
disk file path (.img,.qcow2,.vdi,.vera,.luk). If inexistent, it is proposed to create it.
.TP
overlay path
<upper_dir>><lower_dir>
an overlay file system where the upper directory and the lower directory are separated by '>'.
When there are multiple lower dirs, the lowest is always put at the right most position and
all dirs are separated by '>' as well.
Note: The 'work' directory as documented for overlay systems is transparently created at the same level dir as 'upperdir'
.TP
ADB URL
adb://usb
.TP
NFS URL
nfs://<host>:<remote_dir>
.TP
FTP URL
ftp://[<login>@]<host>[:<port>]
.TP
SSH URL
[ssh://]<login>@<host>[:<port>]
.TP
SAMBA URL
[smb:]//[<login>:[<password>]@]<host>/<share>
.TP
UNC address
//<host>/<share>
.TP
HTTP URL
https://<host>. Only https://drive.google.com supported.
.TP
<mount folder>
Target mount point (it is a folder).
.PP
OPTIONS:
.TP
\fB\-\-volume\-name\fR =STRING
The name for an encrypted volume
.TP
\fB\-P\fR, \fB\-\-part\-disk\fR =PART_TYPE_UUID
Partition a disk.
.TP
\fB\-i\fR, \fB\-\-interactive\fR
runs in interactive mode (dashboard)
.TP
